{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771217693999,"sessionID":"ses_39b33d733ffe2qC1Fb1brs4w5Q","part":{"id":"prt_c64ccaf8f001OeTpKdECC69i3I","sessionID":"ses_39b33d733ffe2qC1Fb1brs4w5Q","messageID":"msg_c64cc75f3001tZIhUmKvdsEoAJ","type":"tool","callID":"call_afa6a668b01344fd9980ca05","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Search for error boundaries","prompt":"Search the codebase for any existing error boundary implementation. Look for:\n- ErrorBoundary components\n- Error boundary usage in App.tsx or other components\n- Error handling UI\n- Global error catchers\n\nSearch in src/components and root files. Report what you find.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"task_id: ses_39b335064ffe1ILtbec8nQLsx1 (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\n## Error Boundary Search Report\n\nBased on a comprehensive search of the codebase, here are my findings:\n\n### Summary: No Error Boundary Implementation Found\n\n### What I Searched For:\n1. **ErrorBoundary components** - No files named or containing ErrorBoundary\n2. **Error boundary usage in App.tsx** - Not found\n3. **Error handling UI** - No error boundary fallback UI found\n4. **Global error catchers** - No window.onerror or unhandledrejection handlers\n\n### Detailed Findings:\n\n#### 1. No ErrorBoundary Components\n- No files matching `*ErrorBoundary*` pattern\n- No components using `componentDidCatch` lifecycle method\n- No components using `getDerivedStateFromError` static method\n\n#### 2. App.tsx Analysis (`/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/App.tsx`)\nThe App component is simple with no error handling:\n```typescript\nfunction App() {\n  const [isIntro, setIsIntro] = useState(true)\n  return (\n    <>\n      {isIntro && <IntroOverlay onEnter={handleIntroComplete} />}\n      {!isIntro && <Game />}\n    </>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n#### 3. main.tsx Analysis (`/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/main.tsx`)\nRoot rendering uses `StrictMode` but no error boundary:\n```typescript\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById('root')!).render(\n  <StrictMode>\n    <App />\n  </StrictMode>\n)\n```\n\n#### 4. index.html Analysis (`/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/index.html`)\nNo global error handlers in the HTML file.\n\n### Existing Error-Related Code (Not Error Boundaries):\n\nThe only error-related patterns found were:\n\n1. **Settings Validation Errors** in `SettingsPanel.tsx`:\n   - UI for displaying import errors: `{importError && <div className=\"settings-error\">{importError}</div>}`\n   - JSON parsing error handling with try-catch\n\n2. **Console Error Logging** in various utility files:\n   - `src/lib/audio.ts` - Audio playback error handling with console.error\n   - `src/lib/level.ts` - localStorage error handling with console.warn\n   - `src/lib/logger.ts` - Logger utility using console.error\n   - `src/lib/state.ts` - localStorage error handling with console.error\n\n3. **Error Sound Handling**:\n   - `playFluxErrorSound()` function references (not error boundary related)\n\n### Conclusion:\n**The codebase currently has no React Error Boundary implementation.** Any runtime errors in React components would cause the entire application to crash and display a blank white screen. Consider adding an Error Boundary component to gracefully handle and display errors.\n</task_result>","title":"Search for error boundaries","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39b335064ffe1ILtbec8nQLsx1","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771217661849,"end":1771217693996}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771217722495,"sessionID":"ses_39b33d733ffe2qC1Fb1brs4w5Q","part":{"id":"prt_c64ccafa60013yAH2H55z6bXId","sessionID":"ses_39b33d733ffe2qC1Fb1brs4w5Q","messageID":"msg_c64cc75f3001tZIhUmKvdsEoAJ","type":"tool","callID":"call_8f5313472d4544309ede4332","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Search for accessibility features","prompt":"Search the codebase for accessibility implementations. Look for:\n- ARIA labels and attributes\n- Keyboard event handlers (arrow keys, Enter, Space, Escape, Tab)\n- Live regions (aria-live)\n- Reduced motion CSS (@media (prefers-reduced-motion))\n- Focus management (useFocusEffect, focus trapping)\n- High contrast mode\n\nSearch in all components and CSS files. Report what you find.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"task_id: ses_39b33504affeQD0BvEnNpgprmx (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\nBased on my thorough search of the codebase, here is a comprehensive report on accessibility implementations:\n\n## Accessibility Implementation Report\n\n### 1. ARIA Labels and Attributes\n**Found:** Very Limited\n- Only **one** ARIA attribute found in the entire codebase:\n  - `src/components/UIToggleButton.tsx` (line 13): `aria-label={isVisible ? 'Hide UI' : 'Show UI'}`\n  \n**Missing:**\n- No ARIA roles (no `role` attributes found)\n- No ARIA expanded/pressed states for toggle buttons\n- No ARIA labels for buttons without visible text (e.g., the settings button with gear icon in GlassHUD.tsx)\n- No ARIA live regions\n- No ARIA descriptions or help text\n\n### 2. Keyboard Event Handlers\n**Found:** Limited\n- **Space and Escape keys** - Used for skipping transitions (TransitionOverlay.tsx lines 65, 69; useTransition.ts line 91)\n- **Backtick key** (`) - Opens/closes settings panel (Game.tsx line 99-102)\n- **G key** - Toggles grid lines (Game.tsx line 103-106)\n  \n**Missing:**\n- No arrow key navigation for grid cells\n- No Tab key focus management\n- No Enter/Space key support for clickable elements beyond transitions\n- No keyboard shortcuts for game controls (Start, Stop, Random, Clear buttons)\n- Grid is not keyboard-accessible - users cannot place or remove cells using keyboard\n- No keyboard navigation for settings panel options\n\n### 3. Live Regions (aria-live)\n**Found:** None\n- No `aria-live`, `aria-atomic`, or `aria-relevant` attributes found\n- No screen reader announcements for score updates, phase changes, or game events\n\n### 4. Reduced Motion CSS (@media (prefers-reduced-motion))\n**Found:** None\n- No `@media (prefers-reduced-motion)` queries found in any CSS files\n- All animations and transitions run regardless of user preferences:\n  - Glitch animations (IntroOverlay.css)\n  - Fade/scale transitions (VictoryScreen.css, TransitionOverlay.css)\n  - Pulse/glow animations (LevelStats.css, ScoreDisplay.css)\n  - Hover transitions (GlassHUD.css, SettingsPanel.css)\n\n### 5. Focus Management\n**Found:** Very Limited\n- **focus styles found:**\n  - `SettingsPanel.css` (lines 185, 231, 243): `.settings-slider:focus`, `.settings-select:focus`\n  - `GlassHUD.css` (line 109): `.hud-slider:focus`\n  - **However, many explicitly set `outline: none`** which removes focus indicators\n  \n**Missing:**\n- No `tabIndex` attributes found - interactive elements cannot receive keyboard focus\n- No `useFocusEffect` or custom focus hooks\n- No focus trapping in modals (settings panel, victory screen, transition overlay)\n- No focus restoration after modal closes\n- No visible focus indicators on most buttons\n- No keyboard focus management for the canvas grid\n\n### 6. High Contrast Mode\n**Found:** None\n- No `@media (prefers-contrast)` queries found\n- No high color contrast mode support\n\n### 7. Other Accessibility Features\n\n#### Semantic HTML\n**Found:** Partial\n- Uses `<section>` elements in SettingsPanel.tsx (lines 289, 312, 368, 432, 496, 577, 617)\n- Uses `<h3>` for section titles\n  \n**Missing:**\n- No `<main>`, `<nav>`, `<header>`, `<footer>`, or `<article>` elements\n- Game uses generic `<div>` elements throughout\n\n#### Form Labels\n**Found:** Good\n- SettingsPanel.tsx has proper `htmlFor` associations for all form inputs (19 label/input pairs)\n- All form controls have corresponding labels\n\n#### Alternative Text\n**Found:** None\n- No `alt` attributes for images (though no images were found, only SVGs)\n- No screen reader-only text for providing context\n\n### 8. Summary of Critical Accessibility Issues\n\n**High Priority Issues:**\n1. Grid is completely inaccessible via keyboard - users with motor impairments cannot play\n2. No focus management - buttons and controls cannot be navigated with Tab key\n3. No ARIA labels for icon-only buttons (settings toggle, mode buttons)\n4. No screen reader announcements for important game events (level complete, score changes)\n5. No reduced motion support - animations could trigger vestibular disorders\n\n**Medium Priority Issues:**\n1. Missing focus indicators on many buttons\n2. No focus trapping in modals\n3. No semantic HTML structure\n4. No keyboard shortcuts for game controls\n5. No high contrast mode support\n\n**Low Priority Issues:**\n1. Limited ARIA attributes overall\n2. No skip links for main content\n\n### Recommendations\n\n1. **Add keyboard navigation to the grid** - Allow arrow key navigation and Enter/Space to toggle cells\n2. **Implement focus management** - Add proper tab indices, focus indicators, and focus trapping in modals\n3. **Add ARIA attributes** - Labels, roles, and states for all interactive elements\n4. **Implement reduced motion** - Wrap all animations in `@media (prefers-reduced-motion)` queries\n5. **Add live regions** - Announce important game events to screen readers\n6. **Add keyboard shortcuts** - Bind game controls (Start, Clear, Random, mode switching) to keyboard keys\n7. **Improve semantic HTML** - Use appropriate HTML5 elements\n8. **Consider adding high contrast mode** - Support users with visual impairments\n</task_result>","title":"Search for accessibility features","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39b33504affeQD0BvEnNpgprmx","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771217661875,"end":1771217722493}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771217729444,"sessionID":"ses_39b33d733ffe2qC1Fb1brs4w5Q","part":{"id":"prt_c64ccaf80001ydrxq4Wc5vaNvW","sessionID":"ses_39b33d733ffe2qC1Fb1brs4w5Q","messageID":"msg_c64cc75f3001tZIhUmKvdsEoAJ","type":"tool","callID":"call_afb79493dc55406c8c87028b","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Search for preset system","prompt":"Search the codebase for any existing custom preset functionality. Look for:\n- Save custom preset buttons or functions\n- Custom preset storage in localStorage\n- UI for naming/saving custom presets\n- Any code related to saving user-defined preset configurations\n\nSearch in src/components/SettingsPanel.tsx, src/lib/presets.ts, and any related files. Report what you find.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"task_id: ses_39b335075ffeqrPex96gfQ2jiB (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\nBased on my comprehensive search of the codebase, here's what I found regarding custom preset functionality:\n\n## Summary: NO Custom Preset Functionality Currently Exists\n\nThe codebase currently has **NO** custom preset functionality. Here are my detailed findings:\n\n---\n\n### What EXISTS (Built-in Presets Only):\n\n#### 1. **Preset System** (`src/lib/presets.ts`)\n- Four hardcoded presets: `EASY`, `NORMAL`, `HARD`, `CHAOS`\n- `applyPreset(preset)` - Applies a preset configuration\n- `getPresetDescription(preset)` - Returns human-readable descriptions\n- `getPresetName(preset)` - Returns preset display names\n- All presets are stored in `PRESET_CONFIGS` constant object (lines 3-124)\n\n#### 2. **Preset Type Definition** (`src/types/index.ts`, line 103)\n```typescript\nexport type Preset = 'EASY' | 'NORMAL' | 'HARD' | 'CHAOS'\n```\n- No provision for custom/user-defined presets\n\n#### 3. **UI for Presets** (`src/components/SettingsPanel.tsx`, lines 289-311)\n- Dropdown selector with 4 built-in preset options\n- Displays preset description below selector\n- Located at top of settings panel\n\n#### 4. **Settings Persistence** (`src/components/Game.tsx`)\n- Current settings saved to localStorage: `'gol-expert-settings'` (line 350)\n- Settings loaded from localStorage on initialization (lines 51-56)\n- **Important**: Only saves ONE current ExpertSettings, NOT a collection of named presets\n\n#### 5. **Export/Import** (`src/components/SettingsPanel.tsx`, lines 179-212)\n- `handleExport()` - Downloads current settings as JSON file\n- `handleImport()` - Loads settings from JSON file\n- Allows saving/loading individual configurations as files\n- **Does NOT** create named presets or manage multiple configurations\n\n---\n\n### What does NOT Exist (Custom Preset Features):\n\n❌ **No functions to save custom presets with user-defined names**\n❌ **No UI for naming/saving custom configurations**  \n❌ **No localStorage storage for multiple user-defined presets**\n❌ **No list/delete functionality for custom presets**\n❌ **No way to add custom presets to the preset dropdown**\n❌ **No \"Save as Preset\" button**\n❌ **No preset management interface**\n\n---\n\n### Documentation Confirms This is Intentional:\n\nFrom `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` (lines 1198-1201):\n```markdown\n- [ ] Add custom preset support\n  - Allow users to save current settings as preset\n  - Name and save custom configurations\n  - NOT YET IMPLEMENTED\n```\n\n---\n\n### Related Storage Keys Found:\n\n| Storage Key | Purpose | Location |\n|-------------|---------|----------|\n| `gol-expert-settings` | Stores current ExpertSettings | Game.tsx line 52, 350 |\n| `gol-{key}` | Generic prefix for localStorage storage | state.ts line 77 |\n\n---\n\n### Current Workaround for Users:\n\nThe only way for users to save custom configurations currently is:\n1. Adjust settings manually in the Settings Panel\n2. Click \"Export JSON\" to download the configuration as a file\n3. Later, click \"Import JSON\" to load that file back\n\nThis is a **file-based approach**, not a **named preset system**.\n\n---\n\n### Conclusion:\n\n**The codebase has NO existing custom preset functionality.** All preset-related code is limited to the four built-in presets (EASY, NORMAL, HARD, CHAOS). If custom preset functionality is desired, it would need to be implemented from scratch.\n</task_result>","title":"Search for preset system","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39b335075ffeqrPex96gfQ2jiB","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771217661832,"end":1771217729442}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771217791703,"sessionID":"ses_39b33d733ffe2qC1Fb1brs4w5Q","part":{"id":"prt_c64ccaf77001FQuDKCLIoVD20p","sessionID":"ses_39b33d733ffe2qC1Fb1brs4w5Q","messageID":"msg_c64cc75f3001tZIhUmKvdsEoAJ","type":"tool","callID":"call_66fb5721aafc42108a71f278","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Explore codebase for gaps","prompt":"Explore the codebase comprehensively to identify:\n\n1. Custom preset support in settings panel (ability to save current settings as custom presets)\n2. Error boundary implementation\n3. Input validation coverage\n4. Edge case handling (empty grid, zero flux, invalid levels, corrupted localStorage)\n5. Browser compatibility checks\n6. Keyboard navigation support\n7. Screen reader support (ARIA labels, live regions)\n8. Reduced motion support\n9. Focus management\n\nSearch src/components, src/lib, src/hooks for any existing implementations of these features. Report back what is and isn't implemented.\n\nThis is a research task - read files, search for patterns, don't write code.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"task_id: ses_39b335081ffelk9goAF6tmj3Zw (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\n## Comprehensive Codebase Analysis Report\n\nBased on my thorough exploration of the codebase, here's a detailed report on the implementation status of the requested features:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Custom Preset Support in Settings Panel\n\n**Status: PARTIALLY IMPLEMENTED**\n\n**What IS Implemented:**\n- **Predefined presets:** EASY, NORMAL, HARD, CHAOS (in `/src/lib/presets.ts`)\n  - Each preset includes comprehensive settings for movement detection, scoring, level generation, grid sizing, and audio\n- **Preset selection dropdown** in SettingsPanel.tsx (lines 289-311)\n- **Preset descriptions** displayed dynamically based on selection\n- **Export/Import JSON** functionality for custom configurations (lines 179-212 in SettingsPanel.tsx)\n- Preset application resets the `preset` field on custom modifications (line 227 in SettingsPanel.tsx)\n\n**What is NOT Implemented:**\n- **No ability to save current settings as NEW custom presets** (e.g., \"My Custom Difficulty\")\n- **No preset management UI** (create, rename, delete custom presets)\n- **No preset storage in localStorage** (only expert settings are stored)\n- **No preset sharing** between devices or users\n\n**Files:**\n- `/src/lib/presets.ts` (154 lines) - Predefined preset definitions\n- `/src/lib/settings.ts` - Settings validation and initialization\n- `/src/components/SettingsPanel.tsx` (690 lines) - UI for preset selection\n\n---\n\n### 2. Error Boundary Implementation\n\n**Status: NOT IMPLEMENTED**\n\n**What IS Implemented:**\n- **Try-catch blocks** around localStorage operations (multiple files)\n- **Error handling** in audio engine (try-catch around all sound operations)\n- **Validation functions** to catch invalid inputs\n- **Console error logging** for failures\n\n**What is NOT Implemented:**\n- **No React Error Boundary component** wrapping the application\n- **No fallback UI** for runtime errors\n- **No error reporting service** or user-facing error messages\n- **No graceful degradation** for major failures\n\n**Evidence:**\n- No `ErrorBoundary` class or component found\n- No imports from `react-error-boundary` or similar libraries\n- App.tsx has minimal error handling\n\n**Recommendation:** Implement a React Error Boundary wrapper around `<App />` or `<Game />` component\n\n---\n\n### 3. Input Validation Coverage\n\n**Status: EXTENSIVELY IMPLEMENTED**\n\n**What IS Implemented:**\n\n**Settings Validation (`/src/lib/validation.ts` and `/src/lib/settings.ts`):**\n- **Coordinate validation:** `isValidCoordinate()` checks bounds\n- **Number validation:** `isPositiveNumber()`, `isNonNegativeNumber()`, `isInteger()`, `isInRange()`\n- **NaN checks:** All number validators check `!isNaN(value)`\n- **Clamping utility:** `clamp(value, min, max)` function\n- **RuleSet validation:** Checks born/survive arrays\n- **Grid dimension validation:** Max 1000x1000 limit\n\n**Detailed Settings Validation in SettingsPanel.tsx (lines 11-166):**\n- `validateExpertSettingsDetailed()` with comprehensive error messages for:\n  - Movement detection settings (centroidHistoryLength: 3-10, movementThreshold: 0.1-2.0, minClusterSize: 1-5)\n  - Scoring settings (moverPointsPerGeneration: 1-100, oscillatorPointsPerGeneration: 0-20, scoreMultiplier: 0.1-5.0)\n  - Level generation settings (baseTimeSeconds: 10-120, timeIncrementPerLevel: 0-60, baseFlux: 5-50)\n  - Grid sizing settings (mobileCellSize: 14-24, desktopCellSize: 16-28, minVisibleCells: >= 1)\n  - Audio settings (volume: 0-0.5, waveform enum validation)\n  - Danger zone settings (chaosMultiplier: 0.5-10.0, timerSpeed: 0.5-5.0)\n\n**Import Validation (SettingsPanel.tsx lines 192-212):**\n- JSON parsing error handling\n- Schema validation on imported settings\n- User-friendly error messages displayed in UI\n\n**Edge Case Math Operations:**\n- `Math.max(5, ...)` to prevent negative flux in level generation (level.ts lines 21, 26, 31)\n- `Math.min(value, max)` for clamping\n- `MAX_SAFE_INTEGER` checks in scoring\n\n**What is NOT Implemented:**\n- **No validation for grid data corruption** (e.g., malformed grid arrays)\n- **No validation for extremely large numbers** beyond the ranges specified\n- **No type guards** for complex nested objects at runtime\n\n---\n\n### 4. Edge Case Handling\n\n**Status: WELL IMPLEMENTED**\n\n**What IS Implemented:**\n\n**Empty Grid:**\n- `isGridEmpty()` function in simulation.ts (lines 135-137)\n- `hasCells()` callback in Game.tsx (lines 179-181) used to prevent starting without cells\n- Phase transition blocked if no cells exist (phase.ts lines 36-38)\n- Empty grid can be created via CLEAR button\n\n**Zero Flux:**\n- `canPlaceCell()` checks if `flux.current >= 1` (flux.ts lines 12-14)\n- Flux error sound when trying to place with zero flux (GridInteraction.tsx lines 86-90)\n- Visual feedback with red border for invalid action\n- Flux color changes to red when zero (flux.ts line 53)\n- Flux is always clamped to minimum of 5 in level generation (level.ts lines 21, 26, 31)\n\n**Invalid Levels:**\n- `getCurrentLevelConfig()` returns `null` for out-of-range levels (level.ts lines 83-88)\n- Null checks throughout Game.tsx when using level config\n- Level bounds validated in level.ts (line 84-86)\n\n**Corrupted localStorage:**\n- Comprehensive try-catch in localStorage helpers (state.ts lines 79-113):\n  - `saveToLocalStorage()`: Returns false on failure, logs error\n  - `loadFromLocalStorage()`: Returns defaultValue on failure, logs error\n  - `removeFromLocalStorage()`: Returns false on failure, logs error\n- JSON.parse wrapped in try-catch with fallback\n- localStorage mocked in tests (test/setup.ts)\n\n**Null/Undefined Checks:**\n- Extensive use of optional chaining (`?.`) throughout\n- Default values provided for optional parameters\n- `canvas.getContext('2d')` null check (CanvasGrid.tsx lines 54-55)\n- `audioContext` null checks before all audio operations\n\n**NaN/Infinity:**\n- `!isNaN(value)` in validation functions\n- `Infinity` used as initial value for distance calculations (movement.ts line 103)\n- `MAX_SAFE_INTEGER` cap on scores to prevent overflow (scoring.ts)\n\n**Array Bounds:**\n- `isWithinBounds()` function for coordinate validation (interaction.ts lines 40-47)\n- Bounds checking in simulation using modulo arithmetic for toroidal grid\n\n**What is NOT Implemented:**\n- **No handling for extremely large grids** causing memory issues\n- **No detection of infinite loops** in pattern detection\n- **No quota exceeded handling** for localStorage\n\n---\n\n### 5. Browser Compatibility Checks\n\n**Status: MINIMAL IMPLEMENTATION**\n\n**What IS Implemented:**\n\n**Audio Feature Detection:**\n- Vendor prefix fallback for Web Audio API (audio.ts lines 248-258):\n  ```typescript\n  const AudioContextClass =\n    window.AudioContext ||\n    (window as typeof window & { webkitAudioContext?: typeof AudioContext })\n      .webkitAudioContext\n  ```\n- Fallback if AudioContext creation fails (try-catch)\n- `getContextState()` method to check audio context status\n\n**Canvas Feature Detection:**\n- `window.devicePixelRatio` usage with fallback to 1 (CanvasGrid.tsx line 57)\n- Canvas context null check before rendering\n\n**Responsive Design:**\n- Mobile breakpoint at 768px in multiple CSS files\n- Touch and mouse event handling (interaction.ts)\n\n**What is NOT Implemented:**\n- **No feature detection for modern APIs** (Intersection Observer, Resize Observer, etc.)\n- **No browser-specific CSS prefixes** beyond -webkit-slider-thumb\n- **No fallback for unsupported features** (e.g., if requestAnimationFrame doesn't exist)\n- **No browser version detection**\n- **No graceful degradation for older browsers**\n- **No polyfills** included\n- **No Safari-specific workarounds** beyond webkitAudioContext\n- **No checks for ES6+ features** before using them\n\n---\n\n### 6. Keyboard Navigation Support\n\n**Status: MINIMAL IMPLEMENTED**\n\n**What IS Implemented:**\n\n**Global Keyboard Shortcuts (Game.tsx lines 98-113):**\n- **Backtick (`)**: Toggle settings panel\n- **Key G**: Toggle grid lines display\n- **Space/Escape**: Skip transition overlay (useTransition.ts lines 90-96)\n- Proper `preventDefault()` to avoid browser default behavior\n\n**What is NOT Implemented:**\n- **No tab navigation** through UI elements (no `tabIndex` attributes found)\n- **No arrow key navigation** for grid interaction\n- **No keyboard shortcuts** for placing/erasing cells\n- **No keyboard shortcuts** for HUD buttons (START, STEP, RANDOM, CLEAR)\n- **No keyboard shortcuts** for selecting interaction modes (DRAW/ERASE)\n- **No keyboard shortcuts** for grid size presets\n- **No keyboard shortcuts** for common actions like RESET or SAVE\n- **No focus indicators** visible when using keyboard\n- **No Enter/Space activation** on buttons beyond default browser behavior\n- **No Escape key** to close overlays (except for transitions)\n- **No focus trapping** in modals/settings panel\n\n**Recommendation:** Implement comprehensive keyboard navigation system including:\n- Tab index management for all interactive elements\n- Arrow key navigation for grid interaction\n- Shortcuts for common actions\n- Focus trapping in overlays\n- Visible focus indicators\n\n---\n\n### 7. Screen Reader Support (ARIA labels, Live Regions)\n\n**Status: MINIMAL IMPLEMENTED**\n\n**What IS Implemented:**\n\n**ARIA Labels:**\n- `aria-label` on UIToggleButton (UIToggleButton.tsx line 13)\n- `title` attributes on some buttons\n\n**Semantic HTML:**\n- `<button>` elements used correctly\n- `<select>` elements for dropdowns\n- `<span>` elements for labels and values\n- Semantic structure with `<h1>`, `<h3>` for headings\n\n**What is NOT Implemented:**\n- **No aria-live regions** for dynamic content (score changes, phase changes)\n- **No aria-atomic** attributes for atomic updates\n- **No role attributes** on custom components\n- **No aria-labels** on most buttons (START, STEP, RANDOM, CLEAR, DRAW, ERASE)\n- **No aria-describedby** for additional context\n- **No aria-expanded** for toggleable elements\n- **No aria-pressed** for toggle buttons\n- **No aria-valuenow/aria-valuemin/aria-valuemax** for progress indicators (timer, flux, score)\n- **No aria-disabled** on disabled buttons (using HTML `disabled` attribute instead)\n- **No screen reader announcements** for:\n  - Phase changes (PLANNING → COUNTDOWN → RUNNING → FINISHED)\n  - Score updates\n  - Level completion\n  - Pattern detections (movers, oscillators)\n  - Flux depletion\n  - Error states\n- **No hidden labels** for icon-only buttons (settings gear icon)\n- **No skip links** for keyboard users\n- **No landmark roles** (main, navigation, etc.)\n\n**Recommendation:** Implement comprehensive ARIA support including:\n- Live regions for dynamic announcements\n- ARIA labels on all interactive elements\n- Progress indicators for timer and flux\n- Screen reader-friendly game state announcements\n- Landmark regions for main content areas\n\n---\n\n### 8. Reduced Motion Support\n\n**Status: NOT IMPLEMENTED**\n\n**What IS Implemented:**\n- `prefers-color-scheme: light/dark` support in index.css (line 56)\n- Media queries for responsive design\n\n**What is NOT Implemented:**\n- **No `prefers-reduced-motion` media query** anywhere in CSS\n- **No animation disabling** for users who prefer reduced motion\n- **All animations run regardless of user preference:**\n  - Score pulse animations (ScoreDisplay.css lines 67-85)\n  - Milestone flash animations (ScoreDisplay.css lines 87-112)\n  - Cell birth/death animations (CanvasGrid.tsx)\n  - Transition fade animations (TransitionOverlay.tsx)\n  - Flux count animations (FluxDisplay.tsx)\n  - Button hover transitions (multiple CSS files)\n  - Button scale animations\n- **No respect for OS-level accessibility settings**\n\n**Animations found in CSS:**\n- `transition: all 0.2s ease` - multiple instances\n- `transition: border-color 0.25s` - index.css\n- `@keyframes pulse` - ScoreDisplay.css\n- `@keyframes milestoneFlash` - ScoreDisplay.css\n- Fade in/out animations in various CSS files\n\n**Recommendation:** Add `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)` blocks to disable or simplify all animations\n\n---\n\n### 9. Focus Management\n\n**Status: NOT IMPLEMENTED**\n\n**What IS Implemented:**\n- Standard browser focus management for form elements\n- `disabled` attributes prevent focus on inactive elements\n\n**What is NOT Implemented:**\n- **No manual focus management** with `focus()` or `autoFocus`\n- **No focus restoration** after closing overlays\n- **No focus trapping** in modals/settings panel\n- **No focus indication** styling beyond browser default\n- **No initial focus** on page load\n- **No programmatic focus** on important elements\n- **No focus management** for keyboard navigation\n- **No `tabIndex` attributes** for custom ordering\n- **No `onFocus` or `onBlur` handlers** for focus state tracking\n\n**Evidence:**\n- No `focus()` method calls found in any component\n- No `autoFocus` prop usage\n- No `tabIndex` attributes found\n- No `onFocus/onBlur` handlers found\n- No focus restoration logic after UI state changes\n\n**Recommendation:** Implement comprehensive focus management for accessibility and keyboard navigation\n\n---\n\n## Summary Table\n\n| Feature | Status | Coverage | Notes |\n|---------|--------|----------|-------|\n| Custom Preset Support | PARTIAL | 40% | Has predefined presets but no ability to save custom ones |\n| Error Boundary | NOT IMPLEMENTED | 0% | Has error handling but no React Error Boundary component |\n| Input Validation | EXTENSIVE | 90% | Comprehensive validation for all user inputs |\n| Edge Case Handling | WELL IMPLEMENTED | 85% | Good coverage of empty grid, zero flux, invalid levels, localStorage errors |\n| Browser Compatibility | MINIMAL | 20% | Only has Web Audio API fallback |\n| Keyboard Navigation | MINIMAL | 15% | Only 3 global shortcuts, no tab navigation |\n| Screen Reader Support | MINIMAL | 10% | Only 1 aria-label, missing live regions |\n| Reduced Motion | NOT IMPLEMENTED | 0% | No `prefers-reduced-motion` support |\n| Focus Management | NOT IMPLEMENTED | 0% | No programmatic focus control |\n\n---\n\n## Priority Recommendations\n\n**High Priority (Critical for accessibility/usability):**\n1. Implement React Error Boundary for graceful error handling\n2. Add `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)` to all animations\n3. Implement comprehensive keyboard navigation with tab indices\n4. Add aria-live regions for dynamic content announcements\n5. Add focus management for accessibility\n\n**Medium Priority (Improved user experience):**\n6. Add ability to save custom presets\n7. Add comprehensive ARIA labels to all interactive elements\n8. Add screen reader announcements for game state changes\n9. Expand browser compatibility checks and fallbacks\n\n**Low Priority (Nice to have):**\n10. Add more keyboard shortcuts for common actions\n11. Add focus trapping in modals\n12. Add skip links for keyboard users\n</task_result>","title":"Explore codebase for gaps","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39b335081ffelk9goAF6tmj3Zw","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771217661820,"end":1771217791700}}}}
